"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo — tự trả lời trước</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>ĐN1</strong> — A machine was purchased for $37,000 and depreciated for five years on a straight-line basis under the assumption it would have a ten-year life and a $1,000 salvage value. At the beginning of the machine's sixth year it was recognized the machine had three years of remaining life instead of five and that at the end of the remaining three years its salvage value would be $1,600. What amount of depreciation should be recorded in each of the machine's remaining three years?</li>\n<li><strong>ĐN2</strong> — A company purchased a machine for $75,000 that was expected to last 6 years and to have a salvage value of $6,000. At the beginning of the machine's fourth year the company decided that the machine's estimated useful life should be revised to a total of 10 years instead of 6 years. Also, the salvage value was re-estimated to be $5,500. Straight-line depreciation was used throughout the machine's life. Calculate the depreciation expense for the fourth year of the machine's useful life.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
